  "text": "Veterinarians | Cornell University Veterinary Specialists | Stamford, CT\nSkip to main content\nSearch:\nGo\nSearch Filters:\nThis Site\nCornell\nMenu\nSearch Cornell\n24-Hour Emergency\n(203) 595-2777\nPartner Portal\nAppointments\nPay Online\nDirections\nHome\nMain navigation\nAbout Us\nMission & Values\nOur People\nFAQ\nCareer Opportunities\nServices\nAnesthesiology\nDentistry, Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology & Endoscopy\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nSurgery\nVeterinary Social Work\nLifeline Blood Bank\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nDoctors\nSpecialty\nBentley, Adrienne\nBuriko, Kate\nDreese, Kaitlyn\nEmbriano, Kreig\nForman, Marnin\nGeddes, Alexander\nGonzalez, Anthony\nHackner, Susan\nLee, Bonnie\nLenfest, Margret\nLove, Edwina\nLyons, Bridget\nMazzaferro, Elisa\nMorgan, Oliver\nRoinestad, Karina\nSeller, Stephanie\nStanley, Emma\nWilson, Kendall\nWynne, Rachel Matusow\nZumbo, Brittany\nResidents\nClarke, Zenobya\nDamone, James\nHilfiker, Hailey\nKang, Aileen\nMercado Hernandez, Betzabeth\nPalleti, Neesha\nEmergency\nAndres, Katharine\nDeCillis, Rebecca\nGeisler, Laura\nReznicek, Eryn\nRigoli, Lindsay\nRoche, Michele\nFor Pet Owners\nPatient Registration\nFAQ for Pet Owners\nClient Experience\nOnline Payment Options\nResources\nSuccess Stories\nFor Veterinarians\nPartner Portal\nContinuing Education\nClinical Briefs\nCase Files\nArticles\nRequest Materials\nEducation\nPet Owners\nStudent Externships\nTechnicians\nVeterinarians\nAnnual CE Conference\nClinical Trials\nCanine Studies\nFeline Studies\nGiving\n24-Hour Emergency\n(203) 595-2777\nContact\nIn This Section:\nEducation\nPet Owners\nStudent Externships\nTechnicians\nVeterinarians\nAnnual CE Conference\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nEducation\nVeterinarians\nVeterinarians\nVeterinarians\nCUVS offers unwavering commitment to the professional development of our referring partners.  We currently offer:\nMonthly CE Series\nAnnual all-day CE event\nEducation to Go\nCPR Certification\nMonthly Veterinarian CE Series\nMonthly CE programs are offered at CUVS. These RACE- and NYS-approved lectures are free of charge. For more information, check out our\nCE page\n.\nAnnual All-Day CE Event\nOur annual, all-day CE conference offers multiple clinical and management tracks and 5 to 6 hours of RACE-and NYS-accredited CE per attendee. It is open to doctors, technicians, students, and office managers.\nOur\n15th Annual CE Conference\nwill be held this Spring\n.\nRecorded sessions will be available on demand for 60 days. For more information on this event and for proceedings of previous CE conferences, see our\nContinuing Education page\n.\nEducation to Go\nToo busy to come to one of our CE programs? Or do you have a few individuals in your practice that are interested in a specific topic? Don’t see a topic you like but know of one that your staff is interested in?\nContact us at\nmarketing@cuvs.org\nfor your personalized program at your practice.\nCPR Basic & Advanced Life Support\nThe Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine offers online certificate CPR courses for veterinary professionals, based on the current ACVECC RECOVER CPR guidelines.\nBoth the Basic Life Support course (3 hours) and the Advanced Life Support course (3 hours) are RACE-approved for CE credits. CPR certification by the American College of Veterinary Emergency and Critical Care (ACVECC) is valid for a 2-year period, at which point veterinary professionals are required to complete the recertification courses in order to renew their certification status.\nFor more information, go to\nhttps://recoverinitiative.org/veterinary-professionals/\nShare this:\nmap\n880 Canal St, Stamford, CT 06902\nphone\n(203) 595-2777\nfax\n(203) 595-2778\nemail\ninfo@cuvs.org\nFollow us on:\nCornell University College of Veterinary Medicine\nCareer Opportunities\nUp\nBack to top",
